    en: `Hey, I'm Jens, a sound designer studying at Sonic College. I work across film, podcasts, installations, music, and games. I'm especially interested in how sound can create atmosphere, tell stories, and shape an audience's experience.

I grew up with music and have played instruments since I was six. I have mainly recorded songs as a multi-instrumentalist, playing piano, singing, and playing bass, guitar, and drums. At Sonic College, I have built on these skills and taken them in a new direction: sound design.

I enjoy combining creative ideas with technical craft. My work includes sound design, Foley, SFX, music, mixing, and sound playback. I work comfortably across disciplines and like finding solutions that bring sound and visuals together.

I work primarily with Pro Tools, Ableton Live 11, and QLab, and have experience with both stereo and multichannel productions. Among other projects, I produced the sound for the animated film Godkiller in Dolby Atmos 7.1.2.

I'm going to do my internship at Aarhus Theatre to explore the world of theatre and experience working with sound in a live setting. I'm curious about new ways of working with sound and drawn to projects that leave room for experimentation and treat sound as an active part of the storytelling.`,
